    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d499">

                <pb facs="0682" n="582" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg582"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">251.11 Insull, Samuel/530: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Skinner</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-04-10T13:00:00-05:00">April 10, 1934—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>40. Your 20 April 10, 10 a.m. and 21 April 10, 11 a.m.<anchor n="46"
                        xml:id="d499-f1"/> Export Line management assures Department that <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Exilona</hi> will wait at Izmir until prisoner’s arrival
                    late Friday afternoon. You should therefore make necessary arrangements to have
                    prisoner proceed by that vessel.</p>
                <p>A new Presidential warrant has been issued naming Berry and the master of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Exilona</hi>, W. Habel, as agents to receive prisoner’s
                    surrender. You should prepare certified copies of warrant reading the same as
                    that repeated in Department’s 34 April 6, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="47" xml:id="d499-f2"
                    /> except that it should be addressed to Burton Y. Berry and W. Habel and the
                    date at the end of the document should read “tenth day of April” instead of
                    “fifth day of April”. This new warrant supersedes that issued to Berry.</p>
                <p>The Export Line is obtaining information as to the dates of the vessel’s call at
                    Sicilian ports and at Casablanca and necessary instructions will be sent looking
                    to prisoner’s unmolested passage through those ports.</p>
                <p>However it is suggested that it would be well to take appropriate steps to
                    discourage communication between prisoner and attorneys or agents who might
                    desire to place obstacles in the way of prisoner’s return to United States. Of
                    course such steps should not involve forceful conflict with procedure having
                    color of sanction in local law.</p>
                <p>Department’s 20 April 6, 1 p.m. to Ankara<anchor n="47" xml:id="d499-f3"/>
                    authorized Berry to draw for necessary traveling expenses himself, Crane<anchor
                        n="48" xml:id="d499-f4"/> and prisoner. Upon receipt of anticipated bill of
                    expenses from Turkish Government telegraph details to Department and
                    instructions will be issued to you regarding payment.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
